{title: Saltwater Letters}
{artist: June & the Lighthouse}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[D]Wrote you a letter in the [A]sand last night
[Bm]Tide came and read it be[G]fore the light
[D]Every word I meant to [A]say out loud
[Bm]Washed away into the [G]morning crowd
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]Saltwater [D]letters, [A]never reach the [Bm]shore
[G]Saltwater [D]letters, I [A]don't write you any[D]more
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[D]Gulls are carrying the [A]pieces home
[Bm]Every vowel and every [G]comma flown
[D]Maybe somewhere there's a [A]beach that knows
[Bm]All the things I never [G]got to show
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]Saltwater [D]letters, [A]never reach the [Bm]shore
[G]Saltwater [D]letters, I [A]don't write you any[D]more
{end_of_chorus}
